CSO Housing App — Meeting Notes
Date: November 18, 2026
1. Email Verification
- A company email account is needed for sending verification and receipt emails.
- The team is switching from Resend to Brevo.
- Brevo provides approximately 9,000 emails per month under the planned setup.
- The application should send a verification link that routes the user to the appropriate page and authenticates the session automatically.
- Users should not need to manually enter a verification code.
Email Usage Estimate
- Students will generally receive two emails per service request:
  1. One verification email containing the authentication link.
  2. One receipt email confirming the request.
- The average estimate is therefore two emails per student per request.
Edge Case
- The system must support students who need to use the service more than once per day.
- Request and email limits should not incorrectly prevent a legitimate student from submitting another request when needed.
2. Development Progress
- Figma was used to create front-end prototypes for both:
  - Mobile application layouts.
  - Web application layouts.
- The resident request page should prefill available user information to reduce repeated data entry.
3. CSO Dashboard and Sessions
- The verified session should remain active until the user explicitly clicks the Log out button.
- The CSO dashboard should preserve the authenticated session while the user is working.
